    "body": "Implements the owned DOM tree specified in ADR-007 (`docs/decisions/007-dom-ownership.md`).\n\n## Background\n\nADR-007 decided that our DOM owns its own memory, independent of lexbor.\nlexbor becomes a pure producer: it parses bytes → produces its tree → our\nconverter walks that tree once and builds `honeybee::renderer::dom::Node`\nobjects. After conversion, lexbor's document is destroyed.\n\n## Plan (two commits)\n\n### Commit 1 — Introduce the DOM (pure, no lexbor)\n\n- `src/renderer/dom/node.hpp` + `node.cpp`\n  - `Node` base class — owns children via `std::vector<std::unique_ptr<Node>>`\n  - `Element : Node` — tag name + attributes\n  - `TextNode : Node` — text content\n  - `Document : Node` — root container, `title()` helper\n  - Non-copyable, non-movable (prevents stale `parent_` pointers)\n- `tests/test_dom.cpp` — children, attributes, text_content, title, deep nesting\n- CMake updates\n\n### Commit 2 — Refactor `renderer::html` to produce DOM\n\n- `src/renderer/html/convert.hpp` + `convert.cpp` — `parse(html) -> unique_ptr<dom::Document>`\n- Delete `src/renderer/html/document.hpp` + `document.cpp` (old RAII wrapper)\n- Rewrite body of `src/renderer/html/preview.cpp` to use `parse()` + DOM API.\n  `preview.hpp` signature unchanged → `window.cpp` unchanged.\n- CMake updates\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] New `renderer::dom` namespace builds and passes its unit tests\n- [ ] `renderer::html::parse()` returns a fully-owned DOM (no lexbor pointers escape)\n- [ ] Existing `make_preview()` behavior preserved (same output for same input)\n- [ ] No lexbor header appears outside `src/renderer/html/convert.cpp`\n- [ ] CI green\n\n## Refs\n\n- ADR-007: `docs/decisions/007-dom-ownership.md`\n- ADR-001, ADR-006",
